<figure id="A0.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2504.20964v1/kstate_v6.svg" id="A0.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:381/496;" width="381" height="496"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>
Diverged kernel states in the state-machine specification (<a href="#A0.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ OSVBench: Benchmarking LLMs on Specification Generation Tasks for Operating System Verification" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 7</span></a> of the <span id="A0.F6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sys_close</span> system call (<a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix A Synthesis Challenges ‣ OSVBench: Benchmarking LLMs on Specification Generation Tasks for Operating System Verification" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 9</span></a>).
Nodes labeled “Old” represent the kernel state prior to the system call’s execution, while nodes labeled “New1” or “New2” depict the potential kernel states following its successful completion. Rhombus-shaped nodes signify the conditions defined in the specification.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A0.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>The state-machine specification of syscall <span id="A0.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sys_close</span> <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix A Synthesis Challenges ‣ OSVBench: Benchmarking LLMs on Specification Generation Tasks for Operating System Verification" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 9</span></a>. In this context, "old" represents the initial kernel state, while "new1" to "new3" denote the subsequent kernel states.
</figcaption>
<div id="A0.F7.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_align_center ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
